---
title: "Global attributes"
description: "The attributes no primitive owns."
section: Foundations
sectionOrder: 1
order: 5
---

Everything a primitive owns is `data-<primitive>-*`. A few attributes belong to the page instead. Each is named for what it sets and takes the choice as its value.

{% globals /%}

## Theme

On any element, `data-theme="dark"` or `data-theme="light"` pins that scheme for the subtree; it only sets `color-scheme`, so scopes nest and every `light-dark()` token follows. Without one, the page follows the system. The head's theme script sets it on `<html>` from `localStorage.theme` before first paint.

## Navigation and persistence

With `data-navigation="swap"` on `<html>`, a same-origin navigation between two opted-in pages fetches the destination and swaps the whole `<body>` in place. Nothing survives the swap unless it carries `data-navigation-persist="<id>"` on both pages; then the live element moves into the new page with its state and scroll offsets, and its links take `aria-current` from the new page. Adding `data-navigation-persist-mode="scroll"` renders the element from the new page and keeps only its scroll offset, for a region whose content changes per page, such as a sidebar. Reloads, hash changes, downloads, and form posts are never intercepted, nor is a link or form inside `data-navigation="off"`. See [navigation](/api/javascript/navigation/).

## Drag opt-out

`data-draggable="false"` keeps a press inside the element from starting a drag: a [drawer](/api/primitives/drawer/) stays still, a [toast](/api/primitives/toaster/) is not swiped away, and a [carousel](/api/primitives/carousel/) track does not follow the mouse. Use it on a region that needs the pointer for itself, such as a map or selectable text. A bare `data-draggable` does nothing.

## Style guard

`data-style-guard="off"` opts an element out of the [style guard](/api/primitives/style-guard/), which otherwise restores style utilities a legacy script overwrites, and of the CSP fallback.
